{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"739055141759615027","content":"Currently its just a flat plot of land with some grass and trees near the northern edge of town.  Sandi gets out his first jar and starts painting the ground.","created_at":"2020-08-01T17:37:37.871000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"739175019560566866","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"739055141759615027","content":"gil finishes the initial drawing.  it's a large pond (or small lake depending on how you define such things) with some water in it.  within the water is some water plants including white water Lilly's, and bioluminescent algae at the bottom.  doing this in pieces may have taken more time but is well worth the payoff.\n\nhe heads over to the nearby river and uses shape water and mold earth to temporarily divert some of the flow of the river to fill his lake the rest of the way.  he uses speak with animals to encourage many of the fish to follow the new flow of water to a new home.","created_at":"2020-08-01T19:44:44.270000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"739207006996529265","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"739055141759615027","content":"stops the water flow now that the lake is filled with water and fish.  Gil takes the tim to fix the earth, making sure ther is no lasting damage to the flow of the river.\n\nhe then goes to painting with his pigments, painting a small hut to the north east of his lake.  the walls are wooden, the roof slate tiles (it's a 10x10 simple structure)","created_at":"2020-08-01T20:26:43.665000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"739217574105055384","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
